## 2026-10-14 - Three staging defects found by cor_lib's selftest, fixed and re-staged (E-75 candidates)

- Disclosure: my 1 Corinthians staging (recorded above as landed) was not faithful in three ways. cor_lib.py's selftest compares the staged files with greek_lib's independent loaders and failed 2 of 24 checks. No lane had launched and nothing had consumed the staged files, so the blast radius was the staged files and the digests recorded above.
  1. SBLGNT was not byte-faithful. build_greek applied NFC, which canonically maps U+037E GREEK QUESTION MARK to U+003B, rewriting 7 characters in 5 verses (5:13, 6:19, 7:18, 7:21, 7:27). citation_sweep collates against the raw substrate, so a quote taken from the staged file could have failed at the byte tier. RP was unaffected.
  2. WEB cross-references leaked into the English. The NT member carries 18 \x ... \x* notes. The stager had no \x rule, and its generic marker strip left their content (for example "+ 1:19 Isaiah 29:14") inside 18 verses.
  3. WEB word attributes leaked in two verses. The NT member nests \+w ... \+w* inside words of Jesus (11:24-25). The \w rule did not accept the \+ form, so `|strong="G2532"` attributes stayed in the text. This one surfaced only after fix 2, on the re-run.
- Root cause: the stager was ported from Daniel's, whose WEB pass was written and tested on Hebrew Bible members only. Those members carry no \x notes and no \+w nesting, and the OSHB pass never met U+037E. The port assumed the OT shape held for the NT, and its own asserts checked counts, not content.
- Sibling audit (MEASURED): every staged OT *_web_clean.txt (Dan, Eccl, Ezek, Isa, Jer, Lam, Prov, Song) has 0 xref-shaped residue, and every staged OT *_web.usfm has 0 \+w. The OT books are unaffected. Every future NT stager must inherit these three rules; John, Rom, Rev, Heb and Matt will all carry \x and words of Jesus.
- Fixes in 1Cor/_stage_phase0_1cor.py (amended, .pre_8f08f0129648 kept): verbatim build_greek with a tab/CR/LF assert; an XREF rule removing each note whole, counted in the report as web.xref_sites_removed (18); W accepts \+w; and new post-write asserts that re-read the staged RP and SBL from disk and require equality with greek_lib, and that the clean WEB has no backslash, no xref residue, no `="` attribute and the same verse count as greek_lib.
- Re-staged twice with every target pin-guarded CLEAR and a .pre_<sha12> copy kept of every output that changed. The intermediate state (fix 2 without fix 3) also has .pre_ copies. Residue scan of the final clean WEB: no markup, no CR, NFC-stable. CR bytes 0 in rp, sbl, usfm, pmarks and the stage report.
- Unchanged by the re-stage: 1Cor_web.usfm, 1Cor_rp.txt, web_greek_verse_check.json, web_greek_offset_map.json. All counts recorded above stand (437 verses, RP pilcrows 35, WEB starts 87 + 9:12, sigla 419 over 220 verses, RP/SBL differences 218, [fn] 16 over 13 verses).
